{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never produces a received byte, reg_dat_do stays ~0 instead of 0xa5, causing uart timeout and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause in excerpt is reg recv_state declared as [3:1] with no bit0, so states 1-10 are truncated/aliased and receive-complete is unreachable. Thus recv_buf_valid never asserts.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,1 +39,1 @@
-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;", "expected": "tohost PASS (vs FAIL 0xdead), loopback 0xa5 received, uart timeout cleared"}

